WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:06.710
At the end of A Dance with Dragons, and of
Season 5 of Game of Thrones, Jon Snow is stabbed

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:11.760
and seemingly killed by men of the Night’s
Watch. The men do this because Jon, as Lord

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.250
Commander, brings thousands of wildlings south
of the Wall. He tries to unite with them

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.730
against the white walkers, and to save them
from being killed and added to the army of

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.810
the dead. But the Watch has been fighting
wildlings for thousands of years and many

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.460
brothers have deep personal grudges. They
see wildlings as “savages”, and fear

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.390
they’ll destroy the Watch, or at eat all
their precious food come winter. Upset with

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.270
the bold changes Jon makes at the Wall, they
whisper that Jon is “A rebel”, “a turncloak”

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.720
and a traitor. The last straw, in the books,
is when Jon announces a plan to “ride south”

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.830
against Ramsay Bolton in Winterfell to rescue
his half-sister. That’s when the brothers

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:55.800
stab him, “For the Watch”.
So it looks like Jon Snow is dead, and apparently

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.090
not coming back. Game of Thrones is repeating
a lesson they’ve taught us before. Good

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:06.420
guys die. Ned gets beheaded, Robb gets Red
Wedded, Cat gets her throat cut. It seems

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.950
like whenever someone tries to do the right
thing in Westeros, they get screwed over,

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.280
by people like Littlefinger and Roose Bolton.
This has been a pretty bleak season. King’s

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.649
Landing is run by bigoted zealots, creepy
necromancers and fools, and Cersei is ruthlessly

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:26.299
humiliated. Sansa is set up to be all empowered,
but she just gets beaten down by the Boltons.

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:32.469
Arya sets off for grand adventure and becomes
a vicious faceless assassin. Jaime tries to

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:38.049
rescue Myrcella, but he fails and she dies.
Brienne tries to rescue Sansa, but she fails,

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:42.700
and all she achieves is the death of Stannis,
who himself is kind of a good guy until he

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.270
burns his daughter. Bran is forgotten, beyond
the Wall, becoming a psychic tree-boy or something

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.979
and gods know where Rickon is. It’s not
all bad with Daenerys, when she’s not burning

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:57.899
innocent men alive – but she’s still in
Essos, with no sign of going west any time

00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:02.670
soon. In Westeros, it’s like we’re all
out of heroes, all out of hope. The white

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:07.590
walkers look unstoppable, and at this point
some may welcome our new ice demon overlords.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.970
They’re probably preferable to people like
Littlefinger and the Boltons. Some people

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.940
think Jon Snow’s corpse will be added to
the army of the dead, or be converted into

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:21.420
a white walker, to lead it against the living.
It feels like the bad guys have won. Game

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.000
over.
But Game of Thrones is not just a story of

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.830
death and loss. The book series is titled
A Song of Ice and Fire – there are two sides

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:37.570
in this story, there is balance, there’s
hope, and in many ways Jon Snow embodies it.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.200
In the show he’s been clearly set up in
opposition to the darkness, to the leader

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.530
of the white walkers, apparently called the
Night King. Surely you don’t have an awesome

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:50.440
standoff like this without a payoff later
on. And Jon is central to many of the unresolved

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:56.340
mysteries and prophesies of the series. R+L=J,
a very popular and well-supported theory,

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.820
claims that Jon Snow’s parents are not Ned
Stark and an unknown woman, but Ned’s sister

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:05.390
Lyanna Stark and the Targaryen prince,
Rhaegar, which has a lot of big implications

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.210
including maybe giving Jon a claim on the
Iron Throne. The prophecy of Azor Ahai states

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:15.000
that certain signs herald the coming of a
hero of the Lord of Light, someone to drive

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.960
back the white walkers and the long night.
Melisandre believes that Stannis is this hero,

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:25.370
but evidence suggests it may actually be
Jon. However you look at it, Jon Snow has

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.600
unfinished business in Westeros, he may be
this hope that seems to be missing from the

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.820
story. So is there any way he can come back
and finish what he’s started?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:40.080
The answer may be Melisandre. We know from
Beric Dondarrion and Thoros of Myr that red

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.240
priests can bring the dead back to life. We’ve
never seen Melisandre resurrect anyone, but

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.220
in the books she says her magic is becoming
“stronger at the Wall”, and that “she

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:53.870
[can] do things that she ha[s] never done
before”. And in the show, Melisandre visits

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.680
Thoros of Myr, maybe comparing notes on resurrection.
So it’s totally reasonable to think that

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:03.740
Melisandre may be capable of bringing the
dead back to life. And she does take a definite

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:09.210
interest in Jon. In the books, Melisandre
foresees his stabbing, warning Jon of “daggers

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:13.440
in the dark”, and telling him that he’ll
have “grave need” of her, that she’s

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.829
his “only hope”. In the show, she says
some interesting things about her “joining”

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:23.590
[with Jon having] power [to] make life [and]
light”, and she turns up at the Wall conveniently

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:29.340
in time for his stabbing. Melisandre’s actress,
Carise Van Houten, has strongly hinted that

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:34.819
“something’s going to happen” between
Melisandre and Jon after Jon’s stabbing.

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:42.050
All this evidence makes it seem very likely that Melisandre resurrects
Jon Snow – but there may be a cost.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:47.030
We’re told over and over that “only death
can pay for life”, and Dance specifically

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:51.570
emphasises that Melisandre needs king’s
blood to perform her magic. There’s this

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:55.970
whole subplot about Jon sending Aemon Targaryen
and Mance Rayder’s son with Sam and Gilly

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:00.310
down to Oldtown, because Aemon has the blood
of Targaryen kings, and Mance’s son has

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.320
the blood of the king-beyond-the-wall, so
Jon fears Melisandre will want to burn them.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.520
But there’s still someone left at the Wall
with kingsblood – Shireen Baratheon, daughter

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:16.500
of King Stannis. Melisandre might burn Shireen
to resurrect Jon. In the show, Melisandre

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.060
has already burned Shireen, to clear the snows
slowing Stannis. She comes to the Wall soon

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:26.040
after, so maybe in the show she’s still
juiced up with kingsblood magic child sacrifice

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.820
power. In the books, at least, it seems pretty
likely that Melisandre will use the sacrifice

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:37.820
of Shireen to resurrect Jon Snow.
Jon’s resurrection may also involve skinchanging,

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:42.740
which the show calls warging. Warging is the
ability to “enter the mind of [an] animal”,

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.960
like Bran enters the mind of his direwolf
Summer. The three-eyed crow tells Bran that

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.880
if he dies, “part of [him] would remain
in Summer”. In the prologue of Dance, a

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.830
wildling warg, Varamyr Sixskins, tells us
that when a warg dies, they can live a “second

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.759
life” by warging into their animal after
death, and in the prologue, Varamyr does this

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:08.040
– he dies, but lives on in his wolf. Varamyr
also specifically tells us that Jon Snow is

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:13.120
a powerful warg, and that living on in Jon’s
direwolf, Ghost, would be “a second life worthy

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:18.680
of a king”. Jon definitely is a warg, though
he resists it – he accidently enters the

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:23.580
mind of Ghost a bunch of times and this connection
with his wolf grows stronger in Dance – Jon

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:28.270
says Ghost is a “part of him”, that he and
Ghost are “one”, just like Bran says

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:33.389
he and Summer are “one”. Melisandre urges
Jon to “embrace” this “power”, and

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:37.850
tells him he’d “do well to keep [his]
wolf close beside” him. At the end of the

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:42.980
book, after Jon is stabbed, his last word
is “Ghost”. Finally, Melisandre has a

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:48.320
vision of Jon changing from “a man, [to]
a wolf, [to] a man again”. In the show,

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.490
Ghost hasn’t been seen for a while, and
there’s been none of this skinchanging foreshadowing,

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:56.889
so maybe in the show Jon will just be straight-up
resurrected by Melisandre. But in the books,

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:01.470
at least, this evidence strongly suggests
that on his death Jon wargs into his direwolf

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:06.460
Ghost, and later becomes “a man once more”,
probably via resurrection by Melisandre with

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:11.639
the sacrifice of Shireen.
This resurrection fits really well with the

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:17.310
mysteries and prophecies surrounding Jon Snow.
If R+L=J is true, and Jon is the son of Prince

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.229
Rhaegar Targaryen, Jon has some claim on the
Iron Throne. In his vow to the Night’s Watch,

00:07:22.229 --> 00:07:27.639
Jon swears to “wear no crown”, but his
vow says his watch ends with his death. Jon

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:32.380
does die, so he’s surely freed of this oath,
allowing him, after his resurrection, to once

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.979
more take part in the politics of Westeros,
and perhaps to make a claim on the throne. This

00:07:37.979 --> 00:07:41.800
gives new meaning to Varamyr’s statement
that a “second life” in Ghost would be

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:47.340
“worthy of a king”. Jon’s resurrection
also fits with the prophecy of Azor Ahai.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:51.440
Melisandre is starting to realise that the
prophesied hero of the Lord of Light is not

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:55.949
Stannis – it’s Jon. There’s this moment
in the show where you can see it in her face,

00:07:55.949 --> 00:08:01.669
when she realises she’s been supporting
the wrong guy all this time. In Dance, Melisandre “pray[s]

00:08:01.669 --> 00:08:07.289
for a glimpse of Azor Ahai, and [her god]
R’hllor [repeatedly] shows [her Jon] Snow”.

00:08:07.289 --> 00:08:12.040
It looks like Jon is Azor Ahai, and this
resurrection helps him fit the prophesied

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:17.139
signs. It’s said that sacrifice may be required
for the rebirth of Azor Ahai, and the sacrifice

00:08:17.139 --> 00:08:22.650
of Shireen could fulfil that. Other signs
of Azor Ahai include smoke and salt, which

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:27.919
may be provided by the smoke and the tears
of Shireen’s burning. Further, Melisandre

00:08:27.919 --> 00:08:33.360
goes on and on about using kingsblood to wake
dragons from stone. Maybe the kingsblood

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:38.760
is Shireen’s, the stone is Shireen’s greyscale,
her stone-like skin condition, and the dragon

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:44.210
is Jon Targaryen. You might think that’s
kind of a lame symbolic fulfilment of Mel’s

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:48.500
waking dragons from stone, but it’s actually
very very similar to something George R. R.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:53.460
Martin has done before, in his novella The
Mystery Knight. In this story, there’s a

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.370
prediction that a dragon will be born, and
what this ends up referring to is the symbolic

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:03.010
emergence of the young boy Egg as a true
Targaryen, Prince Aegon. And when you also consider

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:07.140
that Melisandre admits that she sometimes
misinterprets her prophecies and visions, and

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:11.360
that they can often be symbolic in nature,
it seems totally possible that Melisandre’s

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.980
talk of waking dragons from stone means the
rebirth of Jon as a Targaryen with the sacrifice

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:22.140
of Shireen. Some people go further with this
idea, suggesting that, after being resurrected,

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:26.870
Jon will sentence Melisandre to death for
the crime of killing Shireen. We know that

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:31.430
Ned always told his sons, and Jon, “that
the man who passes the sentence should swing

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:36.850
the blade”, so Jon would kill the fire
priestess with his Valyrian steel sword Longclaw.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:42.640
Maybe, if he does this, the sword will take
on her flame, becoming Azor Ahai’s prophesied

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:47.990
flaming sword, Lightbringer. This is just
speculation, but if it all happens, it would

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:52.800
fulfil almost every sign of the prophecy of
Azor Ahai, and would neatly tie together a

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:58.510
whole bunch of plot threads.
One more possibility is that when Jon dies

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:04.000
and his spirit enters Ghost, he will have
a vision that reveals R+L=J, the truth of

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:09.010
his parentage. In the Dance With Dragons prologue,
when Varamyr is dying and about to begin his

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:13.940
second life in his wolf, he has this moment
where his “spirit” becomes one with nature,

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:18.670
and he looks out through the eyes of a weirwood
tree. Maybe Jon will have a similar experience

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:22.950
when he dies and begins his second life in
his wolf. The reason why this is important

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:27.430
is that Bran Stark is taught by the “three-eyed
crow” to do the same thing – to leave

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:32.040
his body and become one with nature, and to
see through the eyes of weirwood trees. When

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:37.010
Bran does this, he has visions of the past
– of Ned, and other Starks, and others further

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:41.870
back in the past. So if, when Jon dies, he
experiences being one with nature and the

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.730
weirwoods, as Varamyr does, Bran, who is also
on the weirwood network, might share with

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:51.830
Jon his visions. This might sound unlikely,
but it’s actually already happened. In A

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:56.380
Clash of Kings, Jon has a “wolf dream”,
a warging dream, featuring a “weirwood [with]

00:10:56.380 --> 00:11:01.700
his brother’s face”. This tree-boy figure,
representing Bran, gives Jon a vision of Mance

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:06.779
Rayder’s wildling army. So yeah we’ve
got a bit of an Inception visions-within-dreams

00:11:06.779 --> 00:11:11.160
plus possible time travel sorta thing happening
here, but the important point is that Bran

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:15.920
can give Jon visions by connecting with him
through the warging / greensight / weirwood

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:20.180
network thing. So if Jon becomes one with
the weirwoods when he dies and enters his

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:25.160
wolf, just as Varamyr does, it would totally
be possible for Bran to give Jon a vision,

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:29.540
like he does in Clash. And since Bran’s
visions can see into the past, maybe Bran

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:34.860
will give Jon a vision of his real parents,
Rhaegar and Lyanna, possibly of the secret

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:39.600
marriage they may have had at the weirwood
grove at the Isle of Faces. With Jon’s death,

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:45.390
he may learn the truth of his birth. Again,
this is just speculation, just an idea, but

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:49.459
it would a lot of sense. It would explain
why George R. R. Martin has Jon enter the

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:53.160
mind of his direwolf before returning to his
body, instead of just being resurrected by

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:57.339
Melisandre, and it would give a plot purpose
to all this weird entering-the-weirwoods stuff

00:11:57.339 --> 00:12:02.670
that’s associated with the “second li[ves]”
of wargs, and it would finally reveal R+L=J,

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:06.360
which doesn’t really have any other way
of being revealed unless Howland Reed decides

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:11.709
to finally arrive. And how cool would it be?
This guy not only gets brought back from dead,

00:12:11.709 --> 00:12:16.060
released from his vows, fulfilling an ancient
prophecy of the rebirth of a hero, but is

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:21.519
born again with the knowledge of his true
identity – as Jon Targaryen. It’s all

00:12:21.519 --> 00:12:26.410
very biblical – a man of kinda mysterious
birth goes around saying some sensible things

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:30.560
about loving thy neighbour – like – making
peace with the wildlings – but he gets betrayed

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:35.540
and killed by his friends before a cross – like
don’t tell me that’s not a cross – and

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:42.060
he stays dead for a bit, but then is reborn as
a divine hero. So, yeah, in conclusion, Jon

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:47.180
Snow is Game of Thrones Jesus. Or at least,
there’s evidence that Jon Snow will return, and

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:53.450
that the next book is gonna be a helluva read.
Let’s end there. For the evidence that Jon

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:58.930
is the son of Lyanna Stark and Rhaegar Targaryen,
check out the R+L=J video. For a discussion

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:04.420
of the Azor Ahai prophecy, check out the Azor
Ahai video. For an explanation of magnetoencephalography,

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:09.399
check out the MEG video, cause, ah, yeah,
why not, right? It’s about brain imaging, it’s

00:13:09.399 --> 00:13:13.870
got mind reading and robo-hands in it, you
might like it. Thank you for watching, feel

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:17.320
free to comment what you think will happen
to Jon Snow, and what topic you’d like to

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.350
see splained next.

